    "System.CreatedDate": "2026-09-03T18:08:40.577Z",
    "System.Description": "<h2>What needs to be done </h2> <p>Allow an author to choose whether periodic values are laid out horizontally across columns or vertically down rows. The selected direction is a template-wide setting and must be used by every periodic link created in that template. </p> <p>If the author changes the direction after links already exist, show a clear warning and continue only after explicit confirmation. The confirmed change must clear the affected links using the same behavior as the desktop Report Designer. </p><hr><h2>Existing description and implementation details </h2><div><b>Sequencing note:</b> Logically precedes variable linking (1869322)  orientation should be set before an Author starts linking variables, since changing it later clears existing links. </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Requirements</b> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Set orientation</b> </div><div>Author sets time-series orientation (horizontal/vertical) as a one-time setup decision, early in template creation. </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Destructive change warning</b> </div><div>Changing orientation after variables are already linked clears all existing links in the template. Author must be warned with a confirmation dialog and must confirm before this destructive action proceeds. </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Orientation applies template-wide</b> </div><div>Once set, all periodic variable links in the template follow the chosen orientation  this is a template-level structural setting, not a per-link property. </div>",
    "System.Id": 1869334,
